# NestJS Architecture Rules

## Module Structure

Each feature module **MUST** follow this file structure:

```
src/features/{name}/
├── {name}.module.ts        # Module: imports, providers, controllers
├── {name}.controller.ts    # Controller: route handlers, validation
├── {name}.service.ts       # Service: business logic
└── {name}.repository.ts    # Repository: DB queries (optional)
```

## Module Registration

- Feature modules are imported in `app.module.ts`
- Use `@Global()` ONLY for truly global modules (database, redis)
- Never use `@Global()` for feature modules
- Always export services if they're used by other modules

## Controller Patterns

```typescript
@Controller('{path}')
@ApiTags('{Feature Name}')
export class {Name}Controller {
  constructor(private readonly {name}Service: {Name}Service) {}

  @Post()
  @HttpCode(201)
  @ApiResponse({ status: 201, description: 'Created successfully' })
  async create(@Body(new ZodValidationPipe({schema})) createDto: CreateDto) {
    return this.{name}Service.create(createDto);
  }

  @Get()
  @HttpCode(200)
  @ApiResponse({ status: 200, description: 'List retrieved' })
  async findAll(@Query() query: ListQueryDto) {
    return this.{name}Service.findAll(query);
  }

  @Get(':id')
  @HttpCode(200)
  async findOne(@Param('id', ParseUUIDPipe) id: string) {
    return this.{name}Service.findById(id);
  }

  @Patch(':id')
  @HttpCode(200)
  async update(
    @Param('id', ParseUUIDPipe) id: string,
    @Body(new ZodValidationPipe({schema})) updateDto: UpdateDto,
  ) {
    return this.{name}Service.update(id, updateDto);
  }

  @Delete(':id')
  @HttpCode(200)
  async remove(@Param('id', ParseUUIDPipe) id: string) {
    return this.{name}Service.delete(id);
  }
}
```

## Service Patterns

- Services handle business logic only
- Do NOT directly import Drizzle/DB in services - use repositories
- Throw `BadRequestException` or `NotFoundException` for error cases
- Return data directly (ResponseInterceptor wraps response)
- Use `@Injectable()` decorator

```typescript
@Injectable()
export class {Name}Service {
  constructor(
    private readonly {name}Repository: {Name}Repository,
  ) {}

  async create(dto: CreateDto): Promise<{Name}Interface> {
    // Business logic here
    return this.{name}Repository.create(dto);
  }
}
```

## Repository Patterns

- Repository classes handle all DB interactions
- Inject `DRIZZLE` token for database access
- Use TypeScript types from DTOs for return types
- Keep queries simple and focused

```typescript
@Injectable()
export class {Name}Repository {
  constructor(@Inject(DRIZZLE) private readonly db: DrizzleDB) {}

  async create(dto: CreateDto): Promise<{Name}Interface> {
    const [result] = await this.db.insert(schema.{table}).values(dto).returning();
    return result;
  }
}
```

## Dependency Injection Rules

- Constructor injection ONLY (no `@Inject()` on properties)
- Use `private readonly` for all injected dependencies
- Interface injection via custom providers when needed
- Never use `new Service()` - always use DI
